@startuml 09a_state_application
!include _style.puml
title Application state machine (top level)

[*] --> Booting

state Booting {
  Booting : entry / load default font (GlyphSource), open RecentStore, FfmpegLocator::find()
}
state StartupFailed
StartupFailed : entry / show native error dialog (font missing or unreadable)
StartupFailed : exit  / process ends

state Welcome {
  state WelcomeIdle
  state NewProjectDialog
  state RecentDialog
  [*] --> WelcomeIdle
  WelcomeIdle --> NewProjectDialog : click "Create new project"\n/ modal = NewProject (defaults)
  WelcomeIdle --> RecentDialog : click "Open recent"\n/ modal = RecentProjects (entries checked with Path::exists)
  NewProjectDialog --> WelcomeIdle : Cancel or Esc
  RecentDialog --> WelcomeIdle : Close or Esc
  NewProjectDialog --> NewProjectDialog : Create [form invalid]\n/ show field errors, stay open
  NewProjectDialog --> NewProjectDialog : Create [valid] and save fails\n/ show ErrorModal text inline in the form
  RecentDialog --> RecentDialog : Open [file missing or corrupt]\n/ ErrorModal, entry marked "missing" if NotFound
}

state Editor {
  Editor : entry / viewport.fit(), tool = Paint, brush = '#', planes = {Foreground}, ink = #FFFFFF, fill = #808080, active layer = Layer 1, history empty (clean)
  Editor : exit  / stop playback, drop EditorSession (history, thumbnails, textures)
}

state ClosingFlow {
  state ConfirmUnsaved
  state SavingBeforeClose
  ConfirmUnsaved : entry / pending = CloseProject or QuitApplication
  ConfirmUnsaved --> SavingBeforeClose : choice = Save
  SavingBeforeClose --> ConfirmUnsaved : save failed / ErrorModal, keep pending
}

Booting --> Welcome : resources loaded
Booting --> StartupFailed : font load error
StartupFailed --> [*]

NewProjectDialog --> Editor : Create [valid and file written]\n/ RecentStore.touch, Services.projects.save, new EditorScreen
RecentDialog --> Editor : Open [file decodes]\n/ RecentStore.touch, new EditorScreen
Welcome --> [*] : window closed

Editor --> [*] : window closed [history clean]
Editor --> ConfirmUnsaved : window closed [dirty]\n/ cancel OS close, pending = QuitApplication
Editor --> ConfirmUnsaved : File > Close project [dirty]\n/ pending = CloseProject
Editor --> Welcome : File > Close project [clean]
Editor --> ConfirmUnsaved : open another project from Recent [dirty]\n/ pending = OpenProjectFile(path)

ConfirmUnsaved --> Editor : choice = Cancel
ConfirmUnsaved --> Welcome : choice = Discard [pending = CloseProject]
ConfirmUnsaved --> [*] : choice = Discard [pending = QuitApplication]
ConfirmUnsaved --> Editor : choice = Discard [pending = OpenProjectFile]\n/ replace session with the loaded project
SavingBeforeClose --> Welcome : save ok [pending = CloseProject]
SavingBeforeClose --> [*] : save ok [pending = QuitApplication]
SavingBeforeClose --> Editor : save ok [pending = OpenProjectFile]

note right of Editor
  Inside the Editor the Recent modal is reachable from File > Open recent... (same modal as on the Welcome screen).
  Ctrl+S in the Editor never changes the screen state (see 09b and sequence 18).
end note

@enduml

@startuml 09b_state_editor_modals
!include _style.puml
title Editor screen - modal dialog states (one modal at a time) and playback region

state Editor {

  state "Modal region" as ModalRegion {
    state NoModal
    state ColorPicking
    state SaveDialog
    state Exporting
    state ErrorShown
    state UnsavedPrompt
    state BrushEditing
    state ImportDialog

    [*] --> NoModal

    NoModal --> ColorPicking : click char colour swatch / fill colour swatch / frame background swatch\n/ modal = ColorPicker(target, working = current colour, allow_alpha = target is not the frame background)
    ColorPicking --> NoModal : OK / ApplyColor(target, colour, apply_to_all)
    ColorPicking --> NoModal : Cancel or Esc [nothing changes]

    NoModal --> SaveDialog : File > Save as... / Export...\n/ ffmpeg re-checked
    SaveDialog --> NoModal : Cancel or Esc
    SaveDialog --> NoModal : Save [format = .aspr / .png / .ascii / .aanim] and write ok
    SaveDialog --> ErrorShown : Save [write fails]
    SaveDialog --> Exporting : Save [format = ASCII image sequence or .mp4]\n/ start_ascii_sequence() or start_mp4()
    Exporting --> NoModal : Finished
    Exporting --> NoModal : Cancelled [partial file deleted]
    Exporting --> ErrorShown : Failed
    ErrorShown --> NoModal : OK

    NoModal --> UnsavedPrompt : close project / window close [dirty]
    UnsavedPrompt --> NoModal : Cancel

    NoModal --> BrushEditing : top bar [New...] / [Edit...]\n/ modal = BrushEditor(new brush or copy / existing brush)
    BrushEditing --> NoModal : Save [brush valid]\n/ SaveBrush: BrushStore.upsert, brush becomes the active brush
    BrushEditing --> NoModal : Cancel or Esc
    BrushEditing --> ErrorShown : Save [brushes.json cannot be written]\n/ the brush stays usable until the app closes

    NoModal --> ImportDialog : File > Import file... [file chosen and decoded]\n/ modal = Import(file, fit)
    NoModal --> NoModal : File > Import file... [file dialog cancelled]
    NoModal --> ErrorShown : File > Import file... [file cannot be read or decoded]
    ImportDialog --> NoModal : Cancel or Esc
    ImportDialog --> NoModal : Import | Resize project and import | Import without resizing\n/ ApplyImport -> new layer, one undo step
  }

  --

  state "Playback region" as PlaybackRegion {
    state Stopped
    state Playing
    [*] --> Stopped
    Stopped --> Playing : Play [timeline.len() > 1] and NoModal
    Playing --> Stopped : Pause, edit command, undo/redo, frame clicked, any modal opened
  }
}

note bottom of Editor
  Rules
  - While the Modal region is not NoModal the rest of the UI ignores input (dimmed layer) and playback is stopped.
  - Esc closes ColorPicking / SaveDialog / UnsavedPrompt / BrushEditing / ImportDialog as Cancel. Esc does NOT close Exporting (use the Cancel button) or ErrorShown (use OK).
  - The Playback region is detailed in diagram 11a. The import dialog's own phases are in diagram 11d.
end note

@enduml
